 <151988757+SnowGlow-aww@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:59:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(search): free the finale leader for every pin shape

A finale request with fixed characters, or with fixed cards plus fixed
characters, and no chosen leader still put the first pin in the leader
slot. Patch 0004 only freed fixed-card-only requests, so adding a
character pin that the best deck already met could make the result much
weaker (JP #180 card+character 1848 -> 1741 points, below v0.0.14; JP
#218 1868 against 2138 reachable), and the result depended on the pin
order. The deck-recommend UI describes fixed cards and characters as
"must be on stage" and has a separate leader control.

- Send every finale request that has pins but no chosen leader through
  the per-leader search (renamed search_final_chapter_pinned). Each
  per-leader run already folds all pins into its constraints through
  final_chapter_leader_first.
- Restrict leader candidates to pinned characters only when fixed cards
  plus fixed characters fill all five slots.
- The brute-force oracle now lets any leader lead when no leader is
  chosen; add one-character, card+character, card+two-character, 3+1
  and 2+3 pin shapes. With the old routing the test fails on the
  two-fixed-characters shape.
